Yeah, I'm that crazy guy who started the "Ascensions, anyone?" and
"Ascension Strategy - UPDATE" threads. I've learnt a lot from you
guys, so thanks for helping.

My current file started off with a mind-boggling build-breaker, an
uncursed +1 polished silver shield on Dlvl:2. I immediately abandoned
all hope of #twoweaponing for the early- to mid-game, not bothering to
pet-test it through sheer excitement.

Credit cloned a bit with the help of a magic whistle, getting around
4k zorkmids before hitting the mines.

Looting "Q - 8 uncursed daggers named pickup" from some happy gnomes,
I had a merry time in the mines, finding a leash and a silver dagger,
which I promptly wielded.

The altar was crossaligned, but I had a lovely time getting all the
gold from the shopkeepers.

Descended a little deeper without incident, and hit the end (wine
cellar). Hit a poly trap, and randomly became a yellow dragon. Since
my usual build was screwed, as reflection was covered by my shield, I
decided to make some babies, and named them Red, Green and Blue.
Assuming three would be enough, I led them around the place, killing
all the enemies with the power of the magic whistle. Unfortunately,
Green met his doom, and was devoured by the cannibalistic Blue
afterwards (who was an adult by that stage). Went back up to Mine
Town.

I had a lack of wands at that stage, and there's only so far daggers
can go. Thus I decided to let my pets kill the plethora of 'keepers,
since I've been told so many times not to kill them myself. Hoping
that Blue would die and I'd get the scales, I kept them fighting.
Unfortunately, Red became another free meal for Blue, leaving me with
one pet. At some point on the way back, I found a bag of win.

I went back up to Dlvl:2, where the mine stairs were, as well as a
coaligned altar. There, I decided to do something you guys would most
likely never do: kill my pet. Blue exhausted a wand of striking and a
near-full wand of magic missile (I know, it was a bad idea). Thus, I
resorted to the silver saber I relinquished from Mr. Captain. He took
a bit of a beating, but went down eventually. Guess what? NO SCALES.

Fairly pissed off, I continued onto Sokoban. I figured I already had
reflection and a bag of holding, so it'd be pointless. But I thought
the strength bonuses and the experience/gold would be useful, so I did
it anyway. I'd found a pyramidal amulet before, and after BUCing it,
I'd been wearing it for a while. Again, guess what I found at the top
of Soko? "x - a pyramidal amulet"

Yes, you read that correctly. Two amulets and a shield of reflection.
What the hell, RNG. Way to make me be flexible.

Descending into the Dungeons, I picked up a stack of odds and ends,
and realized I needed a closer stash than my altar one on Dlvl:2.
Thus, I decorated the first level of Soko with worthless red glass,
made a stash in the top-left corner and safely read some scrolls. Got
ID and enchant weapon revealed, by enchanting and IDing my +1 silver
saber. Also IDed destroy armour (without any on, of course) and light
(woo). Leaving a slew of unnecessary items (forgotten most of them
now), I headed further towards the darkness.

I found Ludios, and proceeded to run very fast away. I also found the
Quest, and decided to leave that for a bit (due to XP:12 mainly).
Descending a bit further, I found an opulent throne room (two no-
effects and then it vanished), an anthill (easy as pie), and the Big
Room. My God, the Big Room.

I ended up falling into it via a pit (not a good start), and then
decided it wasn't a good idea. Zapped a dig downwards, and healed for
a bit, did some unimportant stuff, then went back up and nearly died.
Damn owlbears. Damn prayers for not releasing you from their grasps.
So yeah, I nearly died there. A scrolled teleport saved me
temporarily, and left me near a cockatrice. And I was pissed.

archmage84: Rubber chicken! *kills* *wields by feet* *plays baseball
with enemies*

The Big Room soon became the Big Statue Hall. Shame I had to ruin the
fine art to get items.

Resuming the uneventful descent, I got telecontrol from a tengu after
fighting my way back to the Soko stash. Quite lucky. I'm now
continuing onward, possibly to the Castle for the wand. Depending on
you people, I might to the Quest first, once I get the XP. (I'm XP:13
from a wraith.)

Any advice, comments or issues?

